    "title": "Hackers Expose Flock Camera Data - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Admin ,\n1 days ago Hackers say they yanked a Flock Safety license plate camera off a pole, cracked it open, and handed the guts to journalists. According to a teardown of that dump, one camera logged about 50,200 vehicles and cranked out roughly 1.6 million images in about three weeks. Software on the unit was detecting people, not just plates. Read full article",
